Title: AROS file system: PhysFS platform layer and AmigaDOS paths
Repository: love
Base: def245102c67909f9902095af613b1ae05249b62
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-19
Author: aros-loeve project
Problem: PhysFS has no AROS platform, so love.filesystem did not start ("Failed to initialize filesystem"). LÖVE and PhysFS also assume Unix or Windows paths: std::filesystem and the start-up script do not understand "Volume:drawer/file", and "Volume:" + "/name" names the parent of a volume in AmigaDOS.
Change: New physfs_platform_aros.c: program drawer from GetProgramDir, ENVARC: as the place for a program's own files; POSIX calls stay in physfs_platform_posix.c (its getpwuid lookup is left out on AROS). The directory archiver does not add "/" after "Volume:". LÖVE: full names through Lock and NameFromLock instead of std::filesystem, save directories in ENVARC:LOVE/<game>, parent drawers of "Volume:a/b", and the start-up script takes "Volume:name" as absolute with the leaf "name".
Scope: AROS (all targets); no effect elsewhere
Upstream: candidate (the PhysFS part for icculus/physfs, the rest for love2d/love)
Verification: Built for mainline AROS x86_64 (GCC 10.5, SDK nightly 20261110) with no implicit function declarations; LÖVE 12.0 ran a test game on pool v1-3 (exec 51.17, softpipe) on 2026-11-19: window, canvas, shader, shapes and a clean exit, seven screen pixels exact
Removal: None planned.
---
